          },
          "message": "Squashed commit of the following:\n\ncommit 5027032607cf22c13d563594009a3e863d5f788c\nMerge: d07c10b be47eac\nAuthor: globegitter <markus.padourek@ecosia.org>\nDate:   Tue Oct 23 14:23:39 2018 +0200\n\n    Merge branch 'apply-buildifier-to-bazel-file' of git://github.com/seh/rules_jsonnet into seh-apply-buildifier-to-bazel-file\n\ncommit be47eac5d461ec4dd8f07ee0eba3e63c45de3762\nAuthor: Steven E. Harris <seh@uber.com>\nDate:   Mon Oct 22 14:19:53 2018 -0400\n\n    Apply \"buildifier\" program to \"jsonnet.bzl\" file\n\n    These changes are the automated output of applying the \"buildifier\"\n    program the \"jsonnet.bzl\"\" file to conform to the expected formatting\n    style for Bazel files.\n\ncommit c096d62ebfa79a9a01b9f216e57b089d681ceeee\nAuthor: Steven E. Harris <seh@uber.com>\nDate:   Sun Oct 14 09:50:57 2018 -0400\n\n    Qualify import paths by workspace and package path\n\n    This patch is an adaptation of an earlier one proposed by\n    @mariusgrigoriu in #59.\n\n    Test the \"imports\" attribute over multiple directories.\n\ncommit ce8a6b395b0fa8826b62512b7b5d40d93a9c995b\nAuthor: Steven E. Harris <seh@uber.com>\nDate:   Mon Oct 22 14:00:56 2018 -0400\n\n    Format BUILD file and adjust brittle test\n\n    The \"extvar_files_test_filegroup\" test expects that its\n    \"ext_str_file_vars\" attribute's list will correspond to the \"srcs\"\n    list elements in the \"test_str_files\" filegroup. However, when\n    formatting the BUILD file with the \"buildifier\" tool, the natural\n    ordering of these two lists compromises their alignment.\n\n    To keep them aligned, force an ordering onto the variable names in the\n    \"ext_str_file_vars\" attribute, ensuring that \"0-workspace\" points to\n    the \"WORKSPACE\" file, and that \"1-test\" points to the \"file.txt\" file.",
